 "descripcion": "A woman stood at the motel window holding the key to a room that doesn't exist. Jonah didn't open the door. The end of Room Twelve.\n\nWould you have let her in?\n\nNarrated fiction. New story every week.\n#horror #horrorstories #scarystories #survival #creepypasta",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "The woman at the window was holding the key to room twelve.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "On the key board, hook twelve was empty.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "She tapped the glass with the key. Slow. Patient.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "I didn't open the door. I called room eleven.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "A man whispered, there's a door in my wall. It wasn't there before.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "I said, don't open it. I'm calling the police.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then I heard the ice machine outside. Ice falling, over and over.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The woman stayed at my window until 5 AM. Then she was just gone.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The police found room eleven empty, the bed still made.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "His truck was still in the lot, with the keys inside.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The owner came in at seven, and he wasn't surprised.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "In 1979, he said, room twelve burned. A couple was inside.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The husband had gone out for ice. They never found him.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "So they bricked the room up, and painted over the door.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "At noon, in bright sunlight, line twelve lit up again.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "It was the man from room eleven. Could you bring some ice?",
   "pausa": 0.9
  },
  {
   "texto": "I quit that day. The ad for my job is still up.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
